  "contentHtml": "\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <p><img src=\"https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/et-default-user.svg\" alt=\"Jahnavi T R\">\n                                            \n                                        </p>\n                                                                        \n                                                                                    <ul>\n                                                                                                    <li>\n                                                                                                                                                                            <a>Jahnavi T R</a>\n                                                            \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \n                                                                                                            </li>\n                                                                                                                                                    <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                                                                            </ul>\n                                                                                <ul>\n                                                                                            <li>Published On Sep 24, 2026 at 11:58 AM IST</li>\n                                                                                                                                </ul>\n                                    \n                                                                            \n                                                                        \n                                \n                                \n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p><a href=\"/tag/bengaluru\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bengaluru</a>: Karnataka’s Food Safety and Drugs Administration (FDA) has urged the Centre to regulate prices of essential medical devices to reduce patients’ out-of-pocket expenditure, proposing a national framework to identify essential devices and cap their prices.FDA commissioner <a href=\"/tag/srinivas+k\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Srinivas K</a>, in letters dated Sept 18 to <a href=\"/tag/drug+controller+general+of+india\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Drug Controller General of India</a> (DCGI), <a href=\"/tag/department+of+pharmaceuticals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">department of pharmaceuticals</a> and national pharmaceutical pricing authority (<a href=\"/tag/nppa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NPPA</a>), proposed a <a href=\"/tag/national+list+of+essential+medical+devices\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">National List of Essential Medical Devices</a> (NLEMD) on the lines of the National List of Essential Medicines.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The proposal covers 24 categories, including devices used in cardiovascular care, respiratory treatment, neurology, obstetrics and gynaecology, ophthalmology, oncology, radiotherapy and kidney care.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>The move comes amid a pricing controversy in Maharashtra, where the state FDA has flagged wide gaps between procurement costs and MRPs of commonly used hospital consumables and sought Centre’s intervention.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Karnataka, however, had raised concerns weeks earlier. In an Aug 4 letter to DCGI Rajeev Singh Raghuvanshi, Srinivas had sought systematic regulation of medical-device pricing and recommended bringing approved devices under the Drugs (Prices Control) Order (<a href=\"/tag/dpco\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">DPCO</a>) framework “to prevent unfair trade margins and protect public interest”.The letter also flagged pricing disparities in medicines, noting that several formulations were being sold at discounts of 30% to 50% from printed MRPs.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>For the proposed NLEMD, Karnataka suggested criteria including clinical importance, public-health relevance, frequency of use, availability of alternatives, risk classification and affordability.FDA said only a limited number of medical devices currently have specific price-control provisions and sought a wider framework to make essential devices more affordable and accessible to patients.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Jahnavi T R</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Jahnavi T R</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/87654367/TNN\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TNN</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Sep 24, 2026 at 11:58 AM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Sep 24, 2026 at 11:58 AM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the ETHealthworld App</a> and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles.</li>\n                    </ul>\n                                            <!-- <div class=\"app-store-contai